## 2. Qualified claims (retained with footnote caveats)

### 2.1 51 Flagship Suites on AA 787-9P
Trade-press sourced (premium-flights.com, not AA primary). Directional; not load-bearing to recommendations. Retained with existing footnote caveat.

### 2.2 Connecting share (60%/two-thirds)
Neither figure has a primary AA document. Correctly disclosed in footnote [^23]. The design-basis midpoint (62.5%) is an analysis construct.

### 2.3 Rent range $100–150/sf/yr
Industry estimate for comparable non-signatory terminal space; no DFW-specific rate is in the evidence. Footnote [^18] retains the "order-of-magnitude" qualifier.

### 2.4 CPE behavioral threshold ~$20–22
Airline-commercial professional judgment; no peer-reviewed or primary source. Retained in the body as professional judgment; footnote [^49] discloses this.

### 2.5 DTW McNamara cost and retrofit history
"Without material retrofit" characterization comes from trade press and aviation enthusiast archives, not audited cost records. Footnote [^7] carries this qualification.

### 2.6 At-grade retrofit range ($204M–$600M)
Derived from analysis of at-grade lounge retrofit displacement cost. Methodology described in footnote [^52].

### 2.7 Decision card cost estimates ([^55]–[^59], [^62])
Engineering and program estimates for decision card costs (Cards 1–6); no independent cost audits exist in the public record. New footnotes [^54]–[^62] added at remediation stage documenting basis and limitations.

### 2.8 O&M reserve 1.5% benchmark ([^60])
Industry practice benchmark; applies broadly to large complex terminal facilities per ACRP research. New footnote [^60] added at remediation stage.

### 2.9 Hub survival list ([^61])
Historical analysis of US hub carrier retention through 2001–2015 consolidation. New footnote [^61] added at remediation stage documenting inclusion criterion.

